# memory and dump (db.c), with Planner (security 9) in Midgaard. memory's counts are the C's allocation counters:
# fresh memory raises them, a thing taken back off a free list doesn't. Its Strings line is the boot's string
# space (17111 strings for the stock world), and its Perms line is a difference kept on purpose, which the
# comparison sets aside (#91, decision 6).
# - memory at boot; then after a new room (Rooms), a two-way link (Exits +2), deleting it (two exits freed) and
#   linking again (the freed ones reused: Exits stays), a reset added, deleted and added again (Resets +1 once),
#   a new mob, object, area and mob program, and a shop assigned, removed and assigned again (Shops +1 once)
# - dump (level 60: Smokegod) writes mob.dmp and obj.dmp (read back), and mem.dmp, whose sizes are a kept difference (not read)
@connect b
Planner
smoke123
@return
@return
scroll 0
goto 3001
memory
edit room create 3036
memory
west link 3001
memory
west delete
west link 3001
memory
done
resets 1 mob 3062
resets 1 delete
resets 1 mob 3062
memory
medit create 3013
done
oedit create 3007
done
aedit create
done
mpedit create 3050
done
memory
medit 3062
shop assign
shop remove
shop assign
done
memory
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
dump
@file mob.dmp
@file obj.dmp
